<section class="panel">
    <h2>How to tune in</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Direct stream</strong>: <a href="https://radio.outofbounds.live/listen/out_of_bounds/radio.mp3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">radio.mp3</a> works in any audio player, and it is the one link on this page that is served straight from the broadcast host.</li>
        <li><strong>Playlist files</strong>: the <a href="https://radio.outofbounds.live/public/out_of_bounds/playlist.pls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">.pls</a> and <a href="https://radio.outofbounds.live/public/out_of_bounds/playlist.m3u" target="_blank" rel="noopener">.m3u</a> files are for players that want a saved station entry.</li>
        <li><strong>Web player</strong>: the station's own <a href="https://radio.outofbounds.live/public/out_of_bounds" target="_blank" rel="noopener">player page</a>, plus the main <a href="https://www.outofbounds.live/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">outofbounds.live</a> site for schedules and announcements.</li>
        <li><strong>In-game</strong>: was Turtle WoW exclusive through the minimap button. That tuner died with the server.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="radio-note"><strong>One caveat about those links.</strong> The playlists, the web player and the now playing feed are served by the same host as the audio, and that host is periodically taken down for maintenance while the team updates the station's site. When that happens the metadata and playlist links stop resolving and the direct stream keeps working. The status line above tells you which state you are in, because it probes the stream itself rather than trusting a cached answer.</p>
